            <ArticleTitle>A novel strategy to overcome resistance in stent placement at lesion site after adequate predilatation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>637-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Resistance was encountered in passing a 3 x 18 mm stent across a lesion in the proximal left anterior descending coronary artery. Successive changes in stent with repeated balloon dilatations did not succeed. Finally, a 9 mm stent was passed across the lesion and deployed at the site of maximal resistance. The 18 mm stent was then placed through this stent. A novel strategy to overcome resistance in the stent passage through the lesion after an adequate balloon predilatation is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
